{"id":24,"date":"2022-11-21T12:25:02","date_gmt":"2022-11-21T12:25:02","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/?post_type=projects&#038;p=24"},"modified":"2025-06-03T06:44:48","modified_gmt":"2025-06-03T06:44:48","slug":"montrose-town-centre","status":"publish","type":"projects","link":"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/project\/montrose-town-centre\/","title":{"rendered":"Montrose Town Centre"},"content":{"rendered":"\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate project-info\">\n        <div class=\"grid\">\n            <div class=\"grid__details\"\">\n\n                \n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Location<\/h5>\n                            <p><p>Montrose, Victoria<\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Client name<\/h5>\n                            <p><p>Yarra Ranges Council<\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Value<\/h5>\n                            <p><p>$1.3 MIL<\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Timeframe<\/h5>\n                            <p><p>2012-2017<\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Contractor<\/h5>\n                            <p><p><a href=\"http:\/\/www.melbcon.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Melbcon<\/a><\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Consultant Team<\/h5>\n                            <p><p>Structural &amp; Civil Engineer &#8211; <a href=\"http:\/\/www.adamseng.com.au\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Adams Consulting Engineers<\/a><br \/>\nServices Engineer &#8211; <a href=\"http:\/\/www.brt.com.au\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BRT Consulting<\/a><br \/>\nAcoustic Engineer &#8211; <a href=\"http:\/\/www.wmgacoustics.com.au\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Watson Moss Growcott<\/a><br \/>\nAccess Consultant &#8211; HSPC-DAC<br \/>\nLandscape Architect &#8211; Landprojects Pty Ltd<br \/>\nGeotechnical Engineer &#8211; Hardrock Geotechnical<br \/>\nTraffic Engineer &#8211; <a href=\"http:\/\/obrientraffic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">O\u2019Brien Traffic<\/a><br \/>\nQuantity Surveyor &#8211; <a href=\"http:\/\/www.plancost.com.au\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Plancost Australia<\/a><br \/>\nBuilding Surveyor &#8211; <a href=\"http:\/\/www.gebuildingsurveyors.com.au\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GE Building Surveyors<\/a><\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Photographer<\/h5>\n                            <p><p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.yelp.com\/biz\/christopher-alexander-photography-blackburn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Christopher Alexander Photography<\/a><\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                \n                \n                \n                                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"grid__text\">\n                <p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Montrose Town Centre is a project that demonstrates the cumulative impact of design details, where the whole is greater than the sum of its parts. It collectively delivers a wealth of much needed community services within the one pleasurable environment.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We were engaged by Yarra Ranges Council to develop a new reception, foyer and library building for Montrose Town Centre. We took a holistic approach considering the neighbouring buildings, the adjacent park and the environmental setting at the foot of the Dandenong Ranges. Our masterplanned design refurbished and linked two free-standing 1980\u2019s Peter Elliott-designed buildings \u2013 a community hall and a library\/meeting building. We also incorporated a new maternal and child health facility and public toilets. Strategically connecting isolated buildings, we created one dynamic and fit-for-purpose facility that meets the diverse needs of the local community.<\/span><\/p>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate two-columns-image\">\n        <div class=\"grid\">\n            <div class=\"grid__image\">\n               <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"619\" height=\"821\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9483-1.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9483-1.jpg 619w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9483-1-226x300.jpg 226w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 619px) 100vw, 619px\" \/>                           <\/div>\n            <div class=\"grid__image\">\n            <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"620\" height=\"821\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9318-1.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"Montrose Town Centre\u2019s entrance door\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9318-1.jpg 620w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9318-1-227x300.jpg 227w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px\" \/>                        <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate full-width-image\">\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1320\" height=\"879\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9470-1.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"Montrose Town Centre\u2019s panoramic view of the facade\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9470-1.jpg 1320w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9470-1-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9470-1-1024x682.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9470-1-768x511.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1320px) 100vw, 1320px\" \/>    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate block-quote\">\n        <div class=\"max-sm:w-full ml-auto w-1\/2\">\n            <div>\n                <blockquote>\n\n                <p>The expanded complex offers an enhanced civic presence to the park. The centralised entry and reception enables a more efficient staffing model and creates a convenient and secure point of access for all users.<\/p>\n\n                \n                <\/blockquote>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate two-thirds-image\">\n        <div class=\"grid\">\n            <div>\n                <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"853\" height=\"569\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9574-1.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"Montrose Town Centre\u2019s rubber floor interiors\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9574-1.jpg 853w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9574-1-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9574-1-768x512.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 853px) 100vw, 853px\" \/>            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate two-columns-text-image\">\n        \n        \n                \n        <div class=\"grid mt-[30px] md:mt-[50px]\">\n            <div class=\"grid__text space-y-12\">\n                <div><p>The form and scale of the new entry building takes its cues from the geometric play of the original architecture, with the addition of strong geometric patterning to identify the new primary entry to the facility.<\/p>\n<p>We worked closely with noted sculptor Anton Hasell who developed a cast bronze public art piece that is integrated with the architecture. The columns at the entry are clad with patterning reminiscent of the tree fern trunks commonly found throughout Dandenong Ranges. The artwork incorporates interactive elements such as cast bronze drums that visitors can \u2018play\u2019 in passing as well as three cast bronze bells which were set into the foyer wall to provide interest and playfulness to the interior.<\/p>\n<p>It is this collection of small gestures and details \u2013 integrations, combinations, orientations, patterns &#8211; that collectively make a big impact. Our design experience means these details do not come at a large cost, yet they lift the mundane into the delightful.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n                            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"grid__image\">\n                 <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"620\" height=\"744\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9660-1.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"bells on the classroom door\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9660-1.jpg 620w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9660-1-250x300.jpg 250w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px\" \/>            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate full-width-image\">\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1320\" height=\"880\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9645-1.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"Montrose Town Centre\u2019s concierge with a view of the library\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9645-1.jpg 1320w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9645-1-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9645-1-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9645-1-768x512.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1320px) 100vw, 1320px\" \/>    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate project-carousel\">\n\n        <div class=\"swiper swiper-block\">\n\n            \n                <div class=\"swiper-wrapper\">\n                    \n                                        \n                        <div class=\"swiper-slide\">\n                            <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"962\" height=\"641\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9325-1.png\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"Montrose Town Centre interior\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9325-1.png 962w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9325-1-300x200.png 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9325-1-768x512.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 962px) 100vw, 962px\" \/>                        <\/div>\n\n                                        \n                        <div class=\"swiper-slide\">\n                            <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"962\" height=\"641\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-3.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"Function room with pink rubber floors and glass walls\